 {"id":"fabro-ad1b","title":"Cite acceptance bullets in implementer verification, don't restate them","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T19:59:23.652Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:36.623Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md, require each PASS line to reference the brief bullet number (e.g. PASS (3)) instead of quoting the criterion, and cap prose before the JSON at 3 sentences. In run 01M0TXPX09279433MGWSWPVVP4, implementer@2 restated all 10 acceptance criteria in full, driving 186 s inference and 0.281 USD (47 percent of run cost). Expected effect: roughly 1.5-2.5k fewer output tokens per pass plus smaller reviewer preambles.","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-1d94","title":"Enforce one edit per file path per tool batch","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T19:59:23.761Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:36.731Z","description":"Add one line to .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md: at most one edit per file path per tool batch; sequence dependent edits across batches. In run 01M0TXPX09279433MGWSWPVVP4 the worker log showed 3 concurrent-write-to-same-file-in-one-batch serializing warnings for main.go, README.md, and fib_test.go. Expected effect: eliminates the write-lock warnings and the silent-ordering hazard they signal, at zero cost.","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-e4fa","title":"Tighten planner sd call economy","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T19:59:23.883Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:36.854Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/planner.md, make the rule conditional and checkable (sd list only if sd ready output is truncated or lacks needed blocker info) and add sd ready --format json to the command table. In run 01M0TXPX09279433MGWSWPVVP4 planner@1 ran sd ready then sd list with byte-identical ~3.3 KB payloads, and used a --format flag on ready not listed in the table. Expected effect: one fewer tracker call and ~10 s less deliberation per cycle while keeping the no-invented-flags rule credible.","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
-{"id":"fabro-e702","title":"Require timeout_ms on compile/test shells and ban placeholder appends in implementer prompt","status":"in_progress","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T20:15:59.086Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T19:16:14.666Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md ('Your job this pass') add two hard rules: (a) any shell call that compiles or tests MUST pass timeout_ms of at least 60000 — run 01M0WWKAQCWZC0Q0JK019H0ZC7's chained append+gofmt+vet+test died at the default 10s with zero output (seq 163-164, 10,345ms, is_error), forcing a blind re-run; (b) never append placeholder code to fix later — the implementer appended a mangled placeholder test via heredoc, then head -n -28 cut the wrong lines leaving a dangling comment, costing ~48s and ~6 wasted calls (a third of its 149.5s stage). Expected effect: implementer pass ~100s instead of ~150s and the silent-timeout failure class eliminated.","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
