 {"id":"fabro-6a5a","title":"Fix PR postlude: disable auto-merge and stop the failing PR-body model call","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":1,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T20:15:59.090Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-09T19:15:43.943Z","description":"In the workflow-owned run settings (CORRECTED PATH: .fabro/workflows/develop/workflow.toml [run.pull_request], line ~53 — NOT .fabro/project.toml, which no longer carries [run.*]) set auto_merge=false — the auto-merge GraphQL call deterministically fails ('Auto merge is not allowed for this repository', enable_auto_merge_if_requested in lib/components/fabro-workflow/src/pipeline/pull_request.rs ~line 609) despite auto_merge=true — and fix or disable the PR-body LLM call, which failed ('No object generated: Failed to parse response as JSON', worker log 16:44:33 in run 01M0WWKAQCWZC0Q0JK019H0ZC7) and fell back to a skeleton. The postlude burned ~53s after the exit node finished (16:43:46 to 16:44:39), 18% of the 293s wall, and emits two warn-level failures every run. NOTE: generate_pr_content in pull_request.rs (~line 490) already runs one structured attempt plus a plain retry with prose salvage; the residual cost is the doomed auto-merge call plus the failing LLM round-trips. Expected effect: run completes ~50s sooner with two fewer recurring warnings. NOTE (design tension to resolve, not transcribe): the workflow.toml comment above the block says auto-merge prevents scheduled runs re-implementing the same seed — weigh that against the planner-side in-flight PR/run check (fabro-06e0/fabro-91ff) which now covers that risk; state the chosen trade-off in the PR body. Partial overlap with open fabro-9f97 (journal-only-diff case); this covers real-diff runs.","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro","closedAt":"2026-09-09T19:15:43.943Z","closeReason":"superseded: basis stale — implemented and merged as PR #107 (run 01M23Q0); user then reverted the auto_merge=false part (auto-merge must stay), and the remaining acceptance criteria (silent no-op enable_auto_merge_if_requested, PR-body call fallback) are present on the base branch"}
 {"id":"fabro-a23f","title":"Make implementer journal report errored or timed-out tool calls","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T20:16:05.689Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:37.192Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/prompts/implementer.md (Journal section) add: a tool call that errored or timed out ALWAYS goes in observations, even when recovered — name the call, the timeout, and the workaround. Run 01M0WWKAQCWZC0Q0JK019H0ZC7's implementer journaled observations as none (seq 187) despite a 10.3s shell timeout, an is_error grep, and a signature change forcing edits at ~28 test call-sites; the signal reached the improve loop only via event-stream archaeology. Complements open fabro-b809 (mandatory painpoints array). Expected effect: friction self-reports on the run where it happens, so prompt fixes surface through the journal pipeline instead of manual analysis.","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
 {"id":"fabro-8d2c","title":"Raise preamble_budget_kb from 24 to 32 — evidence blob detour persists","status":"open","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-09-02T20:16:05.701Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-07T13:23:37.295Z","description":"In .fabro/workflows/develop/workflow.fabro (graph attr, currently 24 after the 12-to-24 raise) set preamble_budget_kb=32. Run 01M0WWKAQCWZC0Q0JK019H0ZC7's 22.1KB evidence capture (seq 209) still rendered as a blob ref in the reviewer prompt (seq 218) because 22.9KB + tester section + context keys (~28KB aggregate) exceeds 24KB; the reviewer recovered via one 102ms read_file, but the same detour produced the false rejection in run 01M0SS23MJM8972CBJD0SP7T4Q. Expected effect: evidence arrives inline in the preamble, one fewer tool round-trip per review, preview-misread mode removed. SUPERSEDES the targets of open seeds fabro-83f9 and fabro-35ab (both still say raise from 12) — close or amend those to avoid triple filing.","labels":["revision"],"assignee":"fabro"}
